# The zoteus fork is its own checkout, cloned by bootstrap.sh — not a submodule,
# not vendored. Nothing under it belongs to this repo's history.
#
# The glob covers siblings deliberately. A second checkout at `fork-stock/`
# appeared untracked, 225 MB of upstream source one `git add -A` away from the
# history this rule exists to keep it out of — the pattern named one directory
# where the reason applies to any of them.
fork/
fork-*/

# The bare mirror `bench/upstream_catchup.py` fetches into. Same reason as
# fork/: upstream's objects are upstream's, and this one is regenerable by
# definition — deleting it costs one clone.
upstream.git/

# Measurement artefacts: regenerable, and large.
bench/*.sqlite
bench/*.sqlite-*
bench/data/
*.log

# Python bytecode from the bench drivers.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-session agent runtime state, not project state — with two exceptions that
# are project state and have to be, because a hook only runs if it is in the tree
# a session opens on. The session-start hook installs the gate's declared
# dependencies so a fresh container can run `make check` without a human
# installing anything (ticket 0498); the settings file is what registers it.
# Everything else under .claude/ stays out.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/

# Review-panel scratch. `/review-pr` writes each perspective's report to
# `.panel/<pr>/` in whatever worktree it runs in, and the durable copy of a
# review is the one posted on the forge. Untracked and unignored, it sat one
# `git add -A` away from landing in a sibling's commit — which is how it was
# found (PR #591, 2026-09-15).
.panel/

# Credential selection for the review seats. Names a variable, holds no secret —
# gitignored anyway, because a .env at a repo root must never become committable
# by someone later putting a value in it.
.env
*.log.txt
node_modules/

# bench/fixtures/fetch_recipe.py's download cache: the fixture corpus's source
# bytes (scanned PDFs, DjVu, wikitext), regenerable from recipe.json. Kept at
# the repo root, same convention as fork/ and upstream.git/ above, so binaries
# never land inside bench/ where check_models.py scans for text.
corpus-cache/

# Built Zotero plugin package, regenerable by bench/zotero-fulltext-plugin/build.sh
*.xpi

# Raw strace output from the egress drivers (bench/probe_getaddrinfo_shape.py and
# its siblings). Regenerable by re-running the probe, and a trace holds this
# machine's paths and pids, which bench/results/** must not carry.
bench/results/**/traces/

# pytest's cache directory. Regenerable by the next `make check`, and it
# appeared untracked at the repo root where every other build artefact above
# is already named.
.pytest_cache/
